<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William II of Holland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1227–1256</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as William II, Count of Holland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William II of Holland was Count of Holland from 1234 and was elected King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> in 1247 by princes opposed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> emperor Frederick II. He began building the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/binnenhof">Binnenhof</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-hague">The Hague</a> as his residence. He was killed in 1256 while campaigning against the West Frisians, before he could be crowned emperor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-ii-of-holland.jpg" alt="William II of Holland" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Titus van der Laars (born 1861 - died 1939) https://www.worldcat.org/identities/lccn-no2005101130/ · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_William_II_of_Holland,_King_of_the_Holy_Roman_Empire_(SVG).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
